Seeded defect for tests/BLite.Wasm.BrowserTests (BrowserScenarioTests)

Hand-made: OpfsPageStorage.FlushAsync forgets its dirty pages. It clears the dirty set and
flushes the OPFS file in the Worker without writing a single page to it, so a checkpoint
persists nothing on OPFS; the WAL (in IndexedDB) still holds every commit, and the checkpoint
truncates it. BLite.Wasm still builds with TreatWarningsAsErrors.

With it applied, the rows that pass on upstream 0450b97 because CheckpointAsync ran before the
reload lose their data on OPFS, and none of them is a registered candidate (Chromium 153,
variant trimmed, 2026-10-17):
    Committed_write_survives_reload Opfs/checkpoint: Expected marker m1 after reload, found ''.
    Typed_write_survives_reload Opfs/checkpoint=True/indexed=False: Expected t1 after reload, found ''.
    Large_database_open_time_and_memory Opfs/20MB: Filled 20971 documents and checkpointed, but the reopened database holds 0.
The IndexedDB rows are unchanged, which places the defect in the OPFS page store.

Reproduce: git apply --ignore-whitespace tests/BLite.Wasm.BrowserTests/seeds/BrowserScenarioTests.opfs-flush-dropped.patch && dotnet test tests/BLite.Wasm.BrowserTests
Restore:   git checkout -- src

The source files mix LF and CRLF line endings; apply with --ignore-whitespace if the patch was
normalised. Never commit the seeded state.

